{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1482172-imperial-mysteries-chronicle","id":1482172,"title":"Imperial Mysteries Chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-28T10:42:12-07:00","id":1482172,"title":"Imperial Mysteries Chronicle","content":"A friend and I have been inspired by Loki and Dr. Strange and the Multiverse of Madness to do an Imperial/Archmage chronicle. Has anyone run a chronicle with an archmage PC? Does anyone have any storyteller or player advice? The PC my friend has in mind is Acanthus, so I was thinking of a story that hops back and forwards in time a lot, like Loki or Dr. Who. Maybe with Mordred, or The Prophet or Ruin as big bads. In a previous chronicle this same character was living in Seatle and dealt with angels, so we have experimented with multiple timelines already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T14:40:55-07:00","id":1482197,"title":"","content":"I'm sure you've already read the 1st ed book &quot;imperial mysteries&quot; to give you a general idea, I've never tried to run a game like that but I think the general thing is to give the players alot of pull in terms of the narrative creating their servants and the NPC's they interact through. I know there is the idea of giving players a certain number of &quot;flashback&quot; points to simply rewrite an event in their favour to represent their superhuman insight. And I know on the discord there were some home-brew rules for 2ed mage archmasters I can't find the link right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4641-pebbles","name":"Pebbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T18:26:08-07:00","id":1482210,"title":"","content":"Time is circles, you heard that by now right ? Hang around any entete with some notion of Time and you eventually hear that adage. The truth is, it used to be, until it never was, now its a square. Perhaps one of the greatest Acts of Imperium in Atlantis was known as <i>Squaring the Circle</i>.<br /> <br /> You see, what used to happen is that a species would be chosen by the Supernal, evolve, makes its marks upon it, make its preparation to leave a legacy and then transcend. Then the next one would be chosen and so on, with multiple civilizations inherting the Earth.<br /> <br /> Before us were the dinosaurs, who evolved into dragons, their own take on post-sentient evolution as we archmages are to mages. They brought people to Atlantis so the next civilization would be built upon their knowledge and their sariras (dragon bones), a legacy that would endure through more cycles. <br /> <br /> But the Atlanteans were prideful and did not want to depend on anyone,much less see their empire fall. So they erased the dragons from history alongside their civilization, its why they are normally impossible to find and why dragon bone only works in areas of Atalntean design. Its a statement of their power being an expression of the city's glory. Then they bound the cosmos to be humanocentric and stop our succesors from existing. <br /> <br /> But somehow traces of this reptile civilization started to show up, one that uses biotechnology and shamanistic occult knowledge. Some echoes of their traditions have started to appear. Recently, their city was pulled from an aborted timeline as a tower amidst the ocean. Someone else has pulled a futuristic Hierachonis from a possible future timeline in response and sealed the area containing both. <br /> <br /> The entrance and archipelago grow more supernatural by the day, those that sail within reported High Speech runes manifesting and clustering as living beings, others say Hierachonis appearing frozen in time. <br /> <br /> We do not know who the major players are or why they are even playing this game, but what we do know is that a full return of that aborted timeline could spell doom for the world. There is many Mysteries to solve and preparations to be made for the expedition, we better start.<br /> <br /> <b>Observation 1:</b> This campaign idea is heavily influenced by Chrono Cross, with Dinopolis being the dinosaur city and Chronopolis being Hierachonis. The Time Devourer, FATE computer, Frozen Flame and the El Nido archipelago in general provide ample inspiration for an archmage sized adventure. <br /> <br /> <b>Observation 2:</b> I would suggest the Dark Rift from Skies of Arcadia:Legends as an inspiration for the treacherous journey in. The alien flora, dimensional portals, the ambient music and even a floating crystal representing a new perfected metal that distorts gravity all help sell the alien feel of it all. <br /> <br /> <b>Observation 3:</b> The Temporal Vortex in Chrono Cross, plus the Trail of Souls and Continent of Mira from Baten Kaitos could provide ideas of what anomalies they would find within. That would be the first challenge of the campaign: Your ship crashed because it needs special modifications to navigate through the Rift. The Quintesses needed can only be found inside. That would help to set the mood for the scale and oddity of what archmages deal with, they are not Travelers anymore, Seekers blaze the corners of reality that anyone else could barely understand.<br /> <br /> <b>Observation 4:</b> Some ideas from the plot of Chrono Trigger could also be used to experience the symptoms of this Mystery in the world, ultimately pointing to a bigger game in the shadows. Then the archipelago arrives, signaling the end of the prelude and start of the escalation into archmage level challenges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-28-2022, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}